   00001| // Rust specification tests → JavaScript cases (R1188-U29, R1188-U30): the
   00002| // rust → js direction of the automated translation, as a recorded workaround
   00003| // until the meta language reads Rust tests.
   00004| //
   00005| // The specification suite under rust/tests/unit/specification/ pins most
   00006| // requirements through the native engine only. Many of its tests have one
   00007| // shape: ask the engine a prompt, then assert that the answer contains (or
   00008| // does not contain) a text, or that the intent is a name. Such a test means
   00009| // the same thing for the browser worker, so this module reads it into a case
   00010| // that a JavaScript runner can ask the worker. A test with any other
   00011| // statement is left to Rust and counted.
   00012| //
   00013| // The reader is a small tokenizer (strings, raw strings, identifiers,
   00014| // punctuation; comments dropped) and a matcher of whole statements.
   00015| 
